{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact G3b configuration head 2a70e1081c68d7f30793d58c4341e369ce44d17b on builder/g3b-register-config-20261103, tree 34b890f4, for request 05c380ce under promise 67c9eb5f and review request 8bde3a05. This approval covers the configuration packet, its source archive, the procedure and the self-hosting rule. It claims no plan, key use, deployment, room or G3 acceptance.\n\nScope. Main 9c7ae712 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head changes docs/self-host.md, the note, five packet files and two manifests, and no product source. The commit-message check passes for both commits. No card path changes. From the gate commit b6e7134a to the head, only the note, the two manifests and one metadata string in source-export.json change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The source archive matches main 9c7ae712, tree 3b5af4b5, exactly. I hashed every member as a Git blob. All 3,946 tracked files match their blob and mode, and the archive holds no other file. Its SHA-256 is 72f84d06…, as recorded. The lockfile equals the one at G3's source afdd8ee5.\n- github-app.json differs from the first G3 file only in registerScope, which is now the placeholder.\n- installed-register-scopes.json lists H3's root sc_7prhc2jy…, G3's root sc_wktzr3u2… and the same placeholder. I matched both roots against sealed host evidence: the H3 crash-recovery logs and the G3 window's fill and staging output.\n- bindings.json matches the first G3 binding file byte for byte (234755b0…). No new Destination or branch enters.\n- The template check imports the production parsers gitHubConfiguration, readInstalledRegisters and oauthPolicy. Both unfilled files refuse. One synthetic root, which deploy.py's pattern also accepts, makes both files read as pinned with all three roots. The maintained celld Worker keeps its name, four Durable Object bindings and three migrations, and registration stays off.\n- The first check named a field that doesn't exist, so it passed without testing anything. Its output stays on the record beside the corrected check.\n- The procedure keeps the fleet prefix, the Worker identity and the earlier roots. It validates the root list before the key read and again at deployment. The planner alone handles the App key. The two refused fresh-owner roots, their recovery custody, the original G3 home and the uncertain Git operation stay untouched. Rollback restores the project retained before the window, not the H3-only project, so it cannot strand the first G3 register.\n- docs/self-host.md now states that a planned register's home creates one room, as ruling c324ad65 requires.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit at b6e7134a reads exit 0. before.json and after.json record the same head, tree 50dd7e0a, lockfile, workspace links and a clean status.\n\nEvidence. The two manifests list 32 public files. All match their sizes and digests and are read-only, both SHA256SUMS files match, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 34 private gate files match their index. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match in the public or the private files. The note names both manifests' SHA-256 values.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each room gets its own register and home, and the installed-roots list keeps every earlier room able to create children.\n\nSecurity: no finding. No key, token or client home enters the packet, and the placeholder refuses until the planner fills it.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One gap in the procedure: preparation step 2 says to verify owned dependency copies inside the new export, but it doesn't say where they come from. The archive holds no node_modules, and deployment step 6 needs node_modules/.bin/esbuild. The G3 procedure named its source and refused any link into another source tree. Planner: before the window, copy an existing dependency directory with the same lockfile, c835dfee…, and refuse any workspace link that leaves the new export.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2